// expect-trap
// expect-trap-at: 19
// BUG-917 regression. Function bodies are IR-only and IR block emission switched
// source mapping off wholesale, so with ONE #line per function and none inside,
// every line in every body mapped to "the function's declaration line, plus the
// offset in the generated C". Every trap therefore named a line that does not
// exist — this file reported line 28. The trap always fired correctly;
// only the location lied, which is why nothing caught it: the number is
// plausible, and the harness discarded stderr entirely.
//
// The padding below is deliberate. The defect scales with distance from the
// function header, so a trap on the FIRST line of a body would have looked
// almost right; this one must be far enough down to be unambiguous.
u32 main() {
    u8[4] a;
    volatile u32 vi = 9;
    u32 i = vi;
    [*]u8 s = a[0..4];
    return s[i];
}
